<<~ ahu #/entry>>

! OODA-HA Runs as a Construction Procedure

The original noosphere OODA-HA governs how a working Lares observes,
orients, decides, acts and reviews the consequences. Within Projection Loom,
that sequence also governs the executable location, epoch and candidate
controllers. Do not confuse this runtime state machine with the developers'
Aftermath/self-review phase; both use the pattern, neither manufactures a
CAD material from a phase name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/five-phases>>

!! Every Active Loop Moves in Order

* ''✶ Observe:'' receive original evidence, current location/lineage, source and code digests.
* ''⏿ Orient:'' establish reference frames, available methods, validity gates, budgets and uncertain sources.
* ''◇ Decide:'' commit an explicit bounded candidate audition or operator-guided course.
* ''▶ Act:'' regrow CAD solids and voids, audit exact constructive validity, score only valid material. A candidate's actual CAD evaluation occurs during its Act, never as post-hoc story.
* ''↺ Hoʻoko / Aftermath:'' inspect measured consequences, preview viable alternatives, allow pet-naming and o-takiage, carry the accepted genome and open another Observe. This phase may investigate itself through another OODA-HA; development Aftermath remains a separate practice.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/phase-anchored-recursion>>

!! Any Phase May Invite Another Loop

An active parent MAY open a child OODA-HA inside Observe, Orient, Decide, Act,
or Aftermath. The child remembers the exact parent phase as an immutable
relationship, pursues its own five-phase investigation and returns a witnessed
consequence. The parent MUST remain in the anchoring phase until all of its
children close. Reentry cannot duplicate previously completed actions.

The code places phase law in `projection_loom/phase_rules.py`:
`PHASES`, `next_phase_allowed`, and `child_phase_anchor` are pure
decisions without durable state or operator power. The sole
`fractal_ooda_ha.OODAJournal` MUST apply phase changes, append actual
receipts and persist consequences; extracting validation MUST NOT create
a second helm. `closed` marks completion after the five phases, not
a sixth OODA action.

The pattern invites recursion when uncertainty, surprising relations, or an
Operator/AI intervention warrants attention; it does NOT require a fixed
five-way fan-out. Session-controlled depth and loop budgets prevent runaway
recursion without hardcoding one architectural decomposition. The runtime
inquiry's Act may carry an operator/AI action receipt; only a tool or executor
performing real work may claim its actual side effects. CAD Act continues to
require real BRep validation.

A child in Aftermath may open its own child. An inquiry can interrupt an
Operator preview review and return to precisely the same candidate choices.
The Operator may intervene during auto-nav at a safe boundary. Pet-names and
whole-location holds remain separate from these ephemeral procedural loop
identifiers. Releasing a pet-name never rewrites loop history.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/two-at-the-helm>>

!! Operator and AI Hold Adjustable Authority

Autonomy moves continuously across manual, co-pilot, auto-nav and full speed.
The Operator MAY pause and review at a safe boundary, steer toward a viable
lineage, pet-name a recognized nameless entity or entire location, request
another direction, or release a name/fork with o-takiage. The AI MAY advise
from observed and validated candidates. An adviser suggestion does not count
as operator consent and does not invent authority over kernel geometry.

The hard gates remain invariant across every autonomy setting: one valid
material body per constructed assembly, declared join and void tests, source
provenance, fixed evidence viewport, finite measurements and durable causality.
The machine checks controls between candidate evaluations and never claims
that a mid-Boolean operation can be forcibly interrupted.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/persistence>>

!! Persist Consequences Rather Than Performance

The location loop contains ordinary epoch and candidate loops; any active
phase may also contain subordinate inquiries. Every
phase records a digest-checked transition, every candidate keeps a separate
CAD result receipt, and operator controls travel through an append-only local
inbox. Reentry resumes completed work; it never reinterprets an old preview
as external evidence. Changed source/code/experiment identity calls for a fork.
A trusted local inbox does not pretend to solve distributed authorization.

CLI auto-nav currently follows deterministic measured-loss selection. A
provider-neutral adviser hook may add actual AI suggestions without bypassing
the operator's steering policy. The machine's procedural OODA-HA operates in
code; naming the phases in comments alone would not satisfy this meme.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/evergreen-capability-composition>>

!! Fractal capability stages under one authority

A candidate's Act MAY open one full child OODA-HA per trusted, versioned capability operator. These children execute real CAD and polymesh generation, carry receipts, and close before the candidate Aftermath. Existing manual, auto-nav, AI adviser, pet-name and o-takiage controls govern those exact compound proposals without a second runner. The location Aftermath MAY itself open a final-gallery OODA-HA, regrowing and auditing scored survivors from across every epoch. The source reference stays provisional unless independently registered.

<<~/ahu>>

